    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1485">

                <pb facs="1606" n="1592" sameAs="frus:frus1944v07/pg1592"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">811.34533/28: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Uruguay</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Dawson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Montevideo</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-01-21T18:00:00-03:00">January 21, 1944—6
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 8:34 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>99. Admiral Ingram and Naval Attaché had this morning with Minister of National
                        Defense<anchor n="7" xml:id="d1485-f1"/> and his advisers conference
                    referred to in my 91, January 19.<anchor n="8" xml:id="d1485-f2"/>
                </p>
                <pb facs="1607" n="1593" xml:id="pg1593"/>
                <p>Naval Attaché reports that Minister was in very receptive mood and told Admiral
                    that Uruguayan authorities are in agreement with his proposal, it being
                    understood that projected air base would be built under Uruguayan direction with
                    assistance of American engineers and equipment, [and] that like other Uruguayan
                    naval facilities, base would be available for use by United States and Allies.
                    Admiral Ingram told Minister that if Navy Department approves, he can have
                    engineers here by middle of February.</p>
                <p>I shall endeavor to obtain confirmation from the President tomorrow.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Dawson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
